 #### Map view rework
 
-Outside the city screen, UI has been reworked too: removed the flag (was needless and cumbersome: better show more buttons instead), added buttons for unit stack and currently selected unit, moved and reordered end turn buttons and other controls, now near the map in a very pretty end turn group with a curved visual effect. Screenshots visible in the other ingame previews.
+Outside the city screen, UI has been reworked too: moved away the flag from production buttons bars (was needless and cumbersome there: better show more buttons instead: moved optionally to top panel as detailed in main changes guide), added buttons for unit stack and currently selected unit, moved and reordered end turn buttons and other controls, now near the map in a very pretty end turn group with a curved visual effect. Screenshots visible in the other ingame previews.
 
 ## UI (Main Sevopedia reworks)

diff --git a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
index 134635415..b4820d3d8 100644
--- a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
+++ b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
@@ -331,6 +331,7 @@ Note: New panels added or modified mostly not mentioned here for concision. See
 - **Main Interface (Common)**: Moved **minimap to the right-edge** for quicker read. Add **details** to most **progress bars**; e.g. in the Tech bar `Fusion: 2245 / 5774 (35)`. Show **chars in the GP bar even if 100%** (e.g. `Great Scientist: Lyons (3) - [RESEARCH_CHAR] 100%`) Change in [GPUtil.py](/Assets/Python/BUG/GPUtil.py) and [CvMainInterface.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMainInterface.py). See [Main interface rework](/README.md#main-interface-rework).
 - **Main Interface (City Screen)**: Enhanced with a new **Great Person +n ICON** information in relevant Buildings' rows; added a new **Specialists Breakdown** and **Culture Breakdown**; added **optional extra rows** in the **Production Chooser Bar** and **optionally hide the unit bar** (`"PlotListPanel"`) (note: does not affect the production chooser outside of the city screen); added **Buttons** (i.e. icons) in the **Production Queue**; fixed some hard anchored items that now **dynamically** adjust to sides' width. **Beautified** it as well: removed the 3 gray bars ("Trade Routes", "Buildings", "Specialists"), increased sides' width, made bonuses columns even in width, and other changes. These changes allow to now display more information and reduce the need for scrolling or hovering. Also **enlarged** the **Bottom-Left** and **Bottom-Right** panels so they align dynamically with the enlarged **Side Panels**. Enhanced the **city bar** and **other bars**, e.g., `Lakamha: 16 - 12372 (4500BC)` or `Growing - 30/43 (4 Turns)`. Split the **Draft group** into hurry controls on the right (and a **new draft button**) and config options on the right. Add building list filtering buttons ("Show All Buildings", "Show Regular Buildings Only", "Show National Wonders Only", "Show World Wonders Only"). And other changes. Change in [CvMainInterface.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMainInterface.py). See also [KI#101](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#101---fixed-base-advciv-bug-of-gp-bar-tooltip-in-city-screen-not-showing-gp-from-obsolete-buildings-yet-seemignly-counting-them-for-the-total-gp-calculation).
 - **Main Interface (Map View)**: **Reordered buttons** (end turn, city change arrows) and wrapped them in a **pretty panel**. Added buttons to unit stack, selected unit. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5503+) Make **left-click on GP bar** open the **corresponding city's city screen**.
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5507+) **Main Interface (civilization flag):** **Removed the civilization flag** from the production buttons bar (next to minimap) to show more buttons instead and have a more efficient display. Instead, added **optional compact top-left civilization flag** (with same preserved BtS hover/click behavior) (if **enabled**, left **top text spacing is shifted to make room for the compact flag**). Unlike base AdvCiv, this **optional flag** is **also visible in city screen** because it does not interfere with bottom city-action buttons. This flag is useful to know player civ, hover for player traits, and click to capital's city screen. Default disabled (tunable) as it can be distracting and undesired.
 - Similarly Beautified and Enhanced the **Technology Advisor** in [CvTechChooser.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvTechChooser.py) so it uses more of the screen while still preserving key information. Players can **tune the advisor's width (4 different options)** in [GlobalDefines_advciv_sas.xml](/Assets/XML/GlobalDefines_advciv_sas.xml). See [Customizable technology advisor width](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Tech_Tree.md#customizable-technology-advisor-width).
 - **Inverted BUG Options** for the **Technology Advisor** and the **Religious Advisor** so they are more accessible. They are now **enabled as a default**, and ticking their box disables them. Rewrote their text for clarity (e.g. "GP Research" -> **"Hide bulbing indicators"**). See [Inverted BUG options](/README.md#inverted-bug-options).
 
@@ -568,7 +569,7 @@ Note: New panels added or modified mostly not mentioned here for concision. See
 - **Melee Unit Combat Type split (rework + balance change):** `UNITCOMBAT_MELEE` is now split into `UNITCOMBAT_MELEE_POLEARM` (melee units that attack from some distance with a lance-like weapon; e.g. Spearmen, Pikemen) and `UNITCOMBAT_MELEE_SHOCK` (close-contact/brawl; e.g. Axemen, Swordsmen, Macemen). For example, after this change, axes still counter polearms but are only slightly stronger than swords; pikemen are no longer worse than axemen which was very odd considering cost and tech requirements difference. Civ-specific variants such as the Babylonian Bowman, or simply the generic Crossbow, now only apply vs. `UNITCOMBAT_MELEE_SHOCK` (i.e., weak vs pikes). **General idea for melee units:** Axeman > Spearman; Crossbow > Axeman/Swordsman/Maceman; Pikeman > Crossbow; Pikeman ≈ Axeman; Maceman > Pikeman. Civ variants retagged to match gear (e.g., Persia Immortal → polearm). **General idea for mounted units:** Spearman > Chariot (`UNITCOMBAT_MOUNTED_MELEE`); generic Horse/Camel Archer (`UNITCOMBAT_MOUNTED_RANGED`) > Spearman; generic Horse/Camel Knights (`UNITCOMBAT_MOUNTED_MELEE`) < Pikemen (`UNITCOMBAT_MELEE_POLEARM`); generic Horse/Camel Cuirassiers > Pikemen (`UNITCOMBAT_MELEE_POLEARM`). See Sevopedia/XML.
 - **Reassignments:** e.g., **Mechanized Infantry** counts as **Armored** (not "Gun") for counter logic.
 - **City defenses** affect all units, including gunpowder and later. See `bIgnoreBuildingDefense` in `CIV4UnitInfos.xml`.
-- **Collateral** values normalized (fixed cases like **Stealth Bomber** having higher base collateral than its limit). Most units now show a **collateral damage limit** (starting at 0 for many). **Collateral promotions 1/2** are broadly available where eligible. Info shown in Sevopedia (Unit chart/Special Abilities) and unit hover panels.
+- **Collateral** values normalized (fixed cases like **Stealth Bomber** having higher base collateral than its limit). Most units now show a **collateral damage limit** (starting at 0 for many) ((Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5506+) hidden for civilian units since they don't use it). **Collateral promotions 1/2** are broadly available where eligible. Info shown in Sevopedia (Unit chart/Special Abilities) and unit hover panels.
 - **Promotions retuned:**
   - Some buffed (e.g., **Woodsman**), some reworked/nerfed (e.g., **Hills Master 2 and 3**), some prereqs changed (e.g., **Archers** can take **City Bombard**; **Logistics** (formerly Commando) requires **Combat 1** or **City Raider 1**; higher-tier promotions (**City Raider/Garrison/First Strike 3**) also need **Combat 2**).
   - **Logistics** now at **The Wheel** (was Military Science).

